      "explanation": "The doctor actively screened for all required red-flag symptoms (fever, cough, hemoptysis, dyspnea, night sweats, weight loss, jaundice, dark urine, fatigue, abdominal pain) either directly or by confirming the caregiver's report, and linked them to emergency triggers. No minor error.",
